  "term": "genetics",
  "definition": "Genetics here refers to the area of medicine focused on genes, genomes, and inherited mutations, and on how advances in studying and manipulating them are changing ideas about disease and its prevention or control. It includes efforts to identify inherited genetic changes that contribute to risks for conditions including cancer, developmental, immune, mental, and neurological disorders.",
